   Domain Specific:
     Terraform (HCL)
     Ansible (YAML)
     Dockerfile
     Makefile
     CMake
     Bazel (Starlark)
     Nix
     Guix

   Total: 40+ language families, 150+ runtime variants.


4) Examples

   ex1.py — Simplest Python script
       #!/usr/local/bin/nexus run
       print("Hello, world.")
   Launched directly as: ./ex1.py

   ex1.rs — Simplest Rust program
       #!/usr/local/bin/nexus run
       fn main() { println!("Hello, world."); }
   Launched directly as: ./ex1.rs

   ex1.go — Simplest Go program
       #!/usr/local/bin/nexus run
       package main
       import "fmt"
       func main() { fmt.Println("Hello, world.") }
   Launched directly as: ./ex1.go

   ex1.ex — Simplest Elixir script
       #!/usr/local/bin/nexus run
       IO.puts("Hello, world.")
   Launched directly as: ./ex1.ex

   ex1.js — Simplest Node.js script
       #!/usr/local/bin/nexus run
       console.log("Hello, world.")
   Launched directly as: ./ex1.js

   ex2.py — Polyglot pipeline
       # Nexus Terminal can orchestrate multiple languages in a single
       # pipeline. This example calls a Rust program, feeds its output
       # to a Python analyzer, then to a Go formatter.
       nexus run analyzer.rs | nexus run process.py | nexus run format.go

   ex3.multi — Multi-runtime project
       # Any project directory can contain files in multiple languages.
       # `nexus build` detects each, invokes the correct build tool, and
       # aggregates results.
       project/
       ├── src/
       │   ├── core.rs        (Rust — build engine)
       │   ├── agent.py       (Python — AI layer)
       │   ├── server.go      (Go — network layer)
       │   └── ui.ts          (TypeScript — frontend)
       └── tests/
           ├── test_core.rs
           ├── test_agent.py
           └── test_server.go

       Running `nexus build` compiles all four in parallel, using
       cargo, pip, go, and npm respectively. The user never switches
       tools.

   ex4.hybrid — Cross-language inheritance
       # A single application can span five languages:
       #   Rust handles the build engine
       #   Python handles the AI agent
       #   Go handles the network daemon
       #   Node handles the UI
       #   Bash orchestrates everything
       # Nexus Terminal compiles, tests, packages, and ships the
       # whole thing as a single deployable unit.


